  "scope": "Remaining 41 additional conceptual questions: keys, distractors, assumptions and counterexamples. First substantive pass only, not independent human review or empirical validation.",
  "findings": {
    "utility-reallocation": "Specified smoothly divisible goods: discrete goods can prevent an arbitrarily small expenditure reallocation.",
    "group-markups": "Specified positive constant common MC, interior optima, percentage markup over price and elasticity evaluated at each optimum. This makes the inverse-elasticity rule precise rather than appealing to unspecified demand groups.",
    "positive-consumption": "Specified positive marginal external benefit, no other distortions and interior private/social optima; otherwise corners or offsetting distortions can defeat strict underproduction.",
    "per-unit-monopoly-tax": "Downward demand alone does not guarantee downward MR. Specified downward MR and interior optima so the output comparative static follows.",
    "gini-extremes": "Specified nonnegative incomes and positive mean, avoiding an undefined conventional Gini for an all-zero distribution."
  },
